add("CriticDEvasion", "critic", f"Attack claim D's landed repair at `{DLAND}`. d-count.py's phrase legs pass once the routed wording is gone; a rewording could keep the same over-read. For each of the 18 base instances (list: `git -C {LANE} show {BASE}:reports/round-53/telemetry/declaration-dry-run.txt`... the instance list is in {LANE}/reports/round-53/telemetry/declaration-dry-run.txt), compare the base line with the landed line and judge: repaired, reworded-but-same-defect, or deleted-without-support. Note that the routed item for line 176 ('primitive peoples') was itself wrong: the phrase is on S181's page in the Collins sense; judge whether the landed line 176 lost supported content and whether that harms depth. Run `python3 -B reports/round-53/d-count.py` and `python3 -B reports/round-53/clauses.py --base-tree <an export of {BASE}>` and paste outputs.", ["depth"])
