add("ExecFinalMeasures", "executor", f"Run the round's after-measurements independently. In a sandbox: `git clone -q --shared {LANE} {SCR}/ExecFinalMeasures && git -C {SCR}/ExecFinalMeasures checkout -q {CLAND}`; export the base: `mkdir -p {SCR}/base && git -C {LANE} archive {BASE} | tar -x -C {SCR}/base`. From the sandbox root run `python3 -B reports/round-53/final-measures.py --tree . --lane {LANE} --base-tree {SCR}/base --label falsify-rerun` (the script is in the lane's working copy, not yet committed: copy {LANE}/reports/round-53/final-measures.py and {LANE}/reports/round-53/clauses.py and {LANE}/tools/check-draft-ids.py into the sandbox first, and say so). Paste the full output. Then check each red control really failed for its stated reason, and add two red controls of your own per claim (sandbox only) that the script does not have. Report every command, output and exit code.", ["coverage", "depth"])
