add("MutateAcceptC", "mutation-tester", f"Mutation-test {LANE}/reports/round-53/accept-c.py in a sandbox clone at {SCR}/MutateAcceptC checked out at `{CLAND}` (never edit the lane). At least 10 single-point mutants (drop the sweep exit-code test, drop the missing_from_index test, accept rows!=files, drop the status==mined test, use substring for the S-id lower bound, skip the used-by test, count only top-level files, return 0 on failure, read the wrong SOURCES column, accept an empty citation set). Run each on the landed tree (expect exit 0) and on red copies (README row removed; cited row queued; used-by emptied; a 230th file). Report killed and surviving mutants and the controls that kill survivors.", ["coverage"])
add("MutateDraftIds", "mutation-tester", f"Mutation-test {LANE}/tools/check-draft-ids.py (a new record tool this round; run `python3 -B tools/check-draft-ids.py --selftest` first). In a sandbox at {SCR}/MutateDraftIds (copy the tool and the lane corpus; never edit the lane): at least 10 single-point mutants (drop each of the three rules F1-F3, loosen the registry-id predicate, drop the citation-parenthesis requirement, ignore NEW- ids, return 0 on findings, skip non-linguistics files). Run each with --selftest, on the round-52 tip entry (`git -C {LANE} show 6524184e:{ED}`, expect 11 findings) and on the landed corpus (expect 0). Also try disguised forms the tool may miss (`(S160,-6)`, `(S160 -6)`, `; -6`, en dash). Report killed and surviving mutants and missed forms.", ["calibration"])
add("MutateClauses", "mutation-tester", f"Mutation-test {LANE}/reports/round-53/clauses.py (uncommitted record script; copy it into a sandbox clone at {SCR}/MutateClauses checked out at `{CLAND}`, with a base export of `{BASE}`). At least 8 single-point mutants (C1 ignores removed files, C1 accepts any added path, C2 checks only 'gesture', C3 misses NEW- ids, D1 compares to the wrong file, D2 checks only added ids, return 0 on FAIL). Run each on the landed tree (expect exit 0) and on red copies (an extra file plus a removed one; topic changed; a NEW- token inserted; a D line deleted; a D S-id dropped). Report killed and surviving mutants.", ["calibration"])
add("ScribeGateLines", "scribe", f"Records: assemble the `## Gate` lines for rows S187-S238 for {LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-53.md, in the format of {LANE}/corpus/lessons/round-52.md:41-120 (`- S### — URL — accessed 2026-10-22 — location: \"quote\". Grounds: ... Seat: <SeatName>.`). Source material: the Gate-line drafts in each wave-1 seat report under {LANE}/.ufo/waves/round-53/build/Scribe*.md and ScoutSourceAccess.md, renumbered with {MAP}. One line per quote; keep each quote verbatim and at most 25 words (drop any longer one and say so); one 'Seat:' tag per line; record every challenge met as 'challenge met, not passed' and the route used. List any row with no Gate quote. Output the block ready to paste, then a one-paragraph search-log note (question, where searched, identified and screened, included, excluded with reasons) in the style of round-52.md's `## Search log`.", ["coverage"])
